.el .ds Aq '
.TH "bead resource add" 1  "bead resource add " 
.SH NAME
bead resource add \- Add one or more normalized local resource keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbead resource add\fR [\fB\-\-fencing\-token\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-key\fR> <\fIID\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add normalized resource declarations to an issue.
.PP
The keys are scheduling exclusions in this native workspace only. They are
not distributed locks. A claimed issue holds every declared key as one
atomic set; adding keys to an in\-progress issue requires its lease fencing
token when applicable.
.PP
EXAMPLE:
  bead resource add <ID> \-\-key gpu:0 \-\-key docker:daemon
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-key\fR \fI<KEYS>\fR
Resource key; repeat for multiple keys
.TP
\fB\-\-fencing\-token\fR \fI<FENCING_TOKEN>\fR
Fencing token for a leased in\-progress issue
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
Issue ID
